cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "ICE: Infinite Context Engine"

message: >-
  If you use LSREP, its evaluation methodology, or the reported ICE v2
  evaluation results, please cite the paper below. If you use the ICE
  software or frozen evaluation artifact, please also cite the archived
  software release.

type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Deepesh
    family-names: Sonar
    email: 18deepnar@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1762-4246"
    affiliation: "Thakur College of Engineering and Technology, Mumbai"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Deepnar/ice"

abstract: >-
  ICE is a local-first conversational memory middleware with typed stores,
  retrieval fusion, and dynamic context budgets. The LSREP paper evaluates
  the frozen v2-paper-eval snapshot using 52 checkpoints and 1,211
  observations of 219 distinct probes from four private conversations.
  Mechanism-fidelity and matched LongMemEval analyses bound the measured
  capabilities; several defined paths were defective or unexercised, and
  graph utility was not established. This software citation identifies the
  frozen evaluation version rather than current development on main.

keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - long-term memory
  - large language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge graphs
  - evaluation methodology
  - local-first

